+    *   Map $v$ to an ASCII character $c$ using the range of ASCII codes 32 to 126.
+    *   The mapping is a direct base-95 conversion where each character represents one digit in base 95.
+    *   *Note:* The source implies a direct mapping for single-digit base-95 representation rather than multi-digit expansion, effectively treating the value as a single symbol in a 95-character alphabet [S1, unofficial].
 
